-- The golden corpus gate's NEGATIVE CONTROL.
--
-- A fragment citing a name `stubs/corpus.id` does NOT carry must still fail,
-- or the prelude has stopped discriminating and every "pass" it produced is
-- worthless. Checked with the prelude prepended, exactly the way a §20 block
-- is checked, so it fails for the same reason a block would.
--
-- This exists because the prelude is the one part of the gate that can make a
-- red row green without any compiler change, and §22's lesson is that the
-- gates which reported a confident number were the ones with nothing standing
-- behind the number.
main = (): i64
    nosuchhelper(1)
    0
end
